id: SESS-010
ilities: [integrity]
source: cpm
maturity: 2
action: block
title: Insecure cookie configuration (session hijacking risk)
category: security
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .ts .js .py .java .rb
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/
patterns:
  - regex: httpOnly\s*:\s*false
    message: "Cookie httpOnly:false — JavaScript can read session cookies, enabling XSS-based session theft"
  - regex: secure\s*:\s*false
    message: "Cookie secure:false — cookies sent over unencrypted HTTP, enabling network sniffing"
  - regex: sameSite\s*:\s*['"](?:none|None)['"]
    message: "Cookie sameSite:'none' — enables cross-site request forgery (CSRF) attacks"
fix: Set httpOnly: true, secure: true, sameSite: 'strict' (or 'lax') for session cookies.
